// @version=6
// MCP Fixture Strategy
//
// The strategy the destructive test suites run against. Committed so the
// fixture is reproducible rather than something that happened to be on a
// chart once.
//
// Deliberately trivial and deliberately NOT a research build:
//   - it must produce a non-empty trade book on any liquid symbol, so the
//     report reader has something to read
//   - it must produce BOTH long and short trades, and both winners and
//     losers, so reconciliation and the P&L identity are actually exercised
//   - it must never resemble a candidate strategy, so a result from it can
//     never be mistaken for a research measurement
//
// Commission is set here, not left at zero. Every backtest in this programme
// is priced net; a fixture that reported gross would train the wrong reflex.

strategy("MCP Fixture Strategy",
     overlay              = true,
     initial_capital      = 10000,
     default_qty_type     = strategy.fixed,
     default_qty_value    = 1,
     commission_type      = strategy.commission.cash_per_order,
     commission_value     = 0.11,
     calc_on_every_tick   = false,
     process_orders_on_close = true)

fastLen = input.int(9,  "Fast MA", minval = 1)
slowLen = input.int(21, "Slow MA", minval = 2)
stopUsd = input.float(5.0, "Hard stop (USD)", minval = 0.0)

fast = ta.sma(close, fastLen)
slow = ta.sma(close, slowLen)

goLong  = ta.crossover(fast, slow)
goShort = ta.crossunder(fast, slow)

if goLong
    strategy.entry("FIXLONG", strategy.long, comment = "FIX B UP")

if goShort
    strategy.entry("FIXSHORT", strategy.short, comment = "FIX B DN")

// A hard stop, so the book contains stopped-out losers as well as crossover
// exits. Without it every exit shares one cause and the exit-tag paths in the
// report reader are never exercised.
if stopUsd > 0 and strategy.position_size != 0
    stopPrice = strategy.position_size > 0
         ? strategy.position_avg_price - stopUsd
         : strategy.position_avg_price + stopUsd
    strategy.exit("FIX HS", stop = stopPrice)

plot(fast, "Fast", color.new(color.aqua, 0))
plot(slow, "Slow", color.new(color.orange, 0))
